facts:
Angles on a **straight line** add to $180^{\circ}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (L) at (-2.6,0);
\coordinate (Rt) at (2.6,0);
\coordinate (U) at (1.3,2.0);
\draw (L) -- (Rt);
\draw (V) -- (U);
\pic[draw, "$a$", angle radius=0.75cm, angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle = Rt--V--U};
\pic[draw, "$b$", angle radius=1.05cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle = U--V--L};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Angles in a **right angle** add to $90^{\circ}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Rt) at (2.6,0);
\coordinate (U) at (0,2.6);
\coordinate (M) at (2.13,1.49);
\draw (V) -- (Rt);
\draw (V) -- (U);
\draw (V) -- (M);
\pic[draw, "$a$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.9] {angle = Rt--V--M};
\pic[draw, "$b$", angle radius=1.0cm, angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle = M--V--U};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Angles **at a point** add to $360^{\circ}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P1) at (60:2.4);
\coordinate (P2) at (175:2.4);
\coordinate (P3) at (300:2.4);
\draw (V) -- (P1);
\draw (V) -- (P2);
\draw (V) -- (P3);
\pic[draw, "$a$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=2.0] {angle = P1--V--P2};
\pic[draw, "$b$", angle radius=1.0cm, angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle = P2--V--P3};
\pic[draw, "$c$", angle radius=1.3cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle = P3--V--P1};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Vertically opposite** angles are equal.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (2.4,1.5);
\coordinate (C) at (-2.4,-1.5);
\coordinate (B) at (-2.4,1.5);
\coordinate (D) at (2.4,-1.5);
\draw (A) -- (C);
\draw (B) -- (D);
\pic[draw, "$a$", angle radius=0.75cm, angle eccentricity=1.9] {angle = A--V--B};
\pic[draw, "$a$", angle radius=0.75cm, angle eccentricity=1.9] {angle = C--V--D};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

